# Build context rules for server/Dockerfile (T-009).
#
# Docker uses this file instead of a root .dockerignore because it sits next
# to the Dockerfile and carries its name
# (https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/, "Dockerfile-specific
# ignore files"). The build context is the repo root (docs/decisions.md,
# T-004), so this file decides what leaves the dev machine.
#
# Allowlist: exclude everything, then let in only what the build needs.
# The last matching line wins.

*

!server/pubspec.yaml
!server/pubspec.lock
!server/bin/
!server/lib/
!packages/api_contract/pubspec.yaml
!packages/api_contract/pubspec.lock
!packages/api_contract/lib/

# Re-exclude, in case they ever appear under an allowed folder.
# Secrets: every .env file, including .env.example (the image never needs it).
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Version control, other packages, and agent files.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
app
.claude
docs
# Build output and tool state.
**/.dart_tool
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.exe
**/*.dill
**/*.aot
